[{:seon.task/name "a-dependency-is-fetched-through-its-owner"
  :seon.task/plan "Done; what exists. Fetching a dependency is an outside-world effect, so it goes through the effect owner like file write-back and git (DECISIONS: Loading code is an effect; the PKG plan, `/Users/sean/src/seon-jolt/notes/archive/option3-PKG-plan.md`). The `:deps` kind in `resources/seon/system.edn` is performed by `seon.fx/resolve-deps`: `{:req {:deps <a deps.edn :deps map>}}` resolved by Jolt's own `jolt.deps/resolve-deps` (no resolver of ours: Jolt fetches `:mvn/version` and `:git/sha`, uses `:local/root`, caches in `.cpcache`), answering `{:value {:roots [absolute source roots]}}` or its one typed error `:seon.fx/unresolved` (in `resources/seon/schemas/seon.problems.edn`, docs/failure-points.md). Jolt answers a missing `:local/root` as a root with no error: task `jolt.deps/a-missing-local-root-is-unresolved`. Measured (fresh HOME, niced): :mvn/version cold 433 ms (one POM and jar over HTTPS), warm 1 ms; :git/sha cold 1433 ms (clone), warm 0 ms; a missing coordinate answered in 440 ms. Not in this task: `add-deps` and `sync-deps` at the REPL, checksums. Wiki: docs/source.md#dependencies."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"jolt.ns/a-built-binary-requires-a-stdlib-namespace-it-did-not-compile"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-dependency-is-resolved-through-its-owner}}
 {:seon.task/name "deps-at-the-repl"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the :deps effect (`seon.fx/resolve-deps`) resolves a deps map through Jolt's `jolt.deps/resolve-deps` and answers the source roots or :seon.fx/unresolved; there is no add-lib or sync-deps at the REPL and no checksum (docs/source.md#dependencies; seon.fx/a-dependency-is-fetched-through-its-owner left them out). Correct, with Clojure's names (clojure.repl.deps): add-lib, add-libs and sync-deps ask the :deps effect through `my.fx/call`, load the answered roots in the agent's process and record the coordinate on its branch; a resolved jar or git tree is checked against a sha256 recorded at its first resolve, and a mismatch is the effect's typed error."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/add-lib-loads-a-resolved-library seon.fx-test/a-changed-artifact-is-refused-by-its-checksum}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-rate-limited-requeue-reads-what-its-owner-sets"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.fx/owner-proc`'s :done arm re-queues a :seon.model/rate-limited outcome behind three guards on values its own procs always set: `(and limited? (:request m))` though `seon.fx/worker-proc` always sends :request; `(or (::qk r) [...])` though `seon.fx/dispatch` sets ::qk on everything it sends a worker; `(if (vector? qk) (second qk) 0)` though qk is always a vector; plus a :seq bump re-insertion under the old key may not need (check). Merged from an agent's attempt (573f12f) with the guards the audit graded C+. Correct: read :request and ::qk as given; a message without them is a defect the contract names. Deletes: the three guards (and the :seq bump if it proves unneeded)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-admit-test/a-rate-limited-model-call-waits-for-the-bucket-and-is-answered}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-effect-opens-a-receipt"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: an agent records an effect only when its answer comes (`seon.agent` writes :seon.fx/status :ok|:error with the outcome), so an agent that dies with a :file, :git or :model call in flight leaves no record that it asked, and a resumed branch cannot tell sent from unsent. v1 committed a receipt before the handler ran, settled it once, and never re-sent it on recovery (~/src/seon/src/seon/effect.clj:1-9). Correct: for a non-idempotent kind, the agent writes :seon.fx/status :open with kind, request and the form's ordinal on its branch before `my.fx/call` sends; the answer settles that entity and links the eval; the reconciler marks a dead agent's open receipt :interrupted and never re-sends it. Foundation for `seon.fx/files-and-shell-for-any-work`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-dead-agents-open-effect-is-interrupted-not-resent seon.fx-test/an-effect-links-its-eval}}
 {:seon.task/name "files-and-shell-for-any-work"
  :seon.task/plan "Seon does any work its user wants (AGENTS §1; owner 2026-10-22). What exists: the effect kinds in resources/seon/system.edn :fx are :echo :file :source :git :deps :build :model; `seon.fx/write-file` writes any path with no prior-digest check; there is no my.fs, my.edit or my.shell. Correct: :fs (read, glob, stat, write with the prior digest as precondition), :edit (exact-span text and line windows) and :shell (argv only, cwd, an env allowlist, a stdin cap, bounded by bytes not a clock) kinds, with my.fs, my.edit and my.shell as thin wrappers over `my.fx/call`. v1's handler policy becomes config keys (:seon.config.fs/*, :seon.config.shell/env-allowlist; v1 src/seon/fs/jvm.clj:21-127, shell/jvm.clj:73). Each function gets a section in docs/agent.md. Deletes: write-file's unchecked path, folded into the :fs write."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.fx/an-effect-opens-a-receipt"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-write-needs-the-prior-digest seon.fx-test/shell-answers-exit-and-digested-output seon.fx-test/shell-sees-only-allowed-env}}
 {:seon.task/name "web-fetch-and-search"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: no :web effect, so an agent cannot fetch a page or search (parity.md gap 11). v1: `my.web/fetch` and `search`, http(s) only, no userinfo in the URL, manual redirects with loop detection, a body cap (~/src/seon/src/seon/web/jvm.clj:42,156,297-334); the search key held by root, named by an env-var config key. Correct: :web-fetch and :web-search kinds in system.edn :fx, the search key read only by root's owner (as `seon.fx/model` reads the model key), with my.web as a wrapper over `my.fx/call`; caps as :seon.config.web/* keys."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.fx/an-effect-opens-a-receipt"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/redirects-are-bounded seon.fx-test/search-key-stays-in-root}}]
